<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Browser "more" popup sheet.

    The menu rows are GROUPED CARDS — the security sheet's shape (see
    its layout header): every row a selectable MaterialCardView on
    colorSurfaceContainerLow, rows of one group 2dp apart with 16dp
    outer / 4dp inner corners, groups 12dp apart. The groups do the
    sectioning, so there are NO hairline rules any more (the flat rows +
    dividers that preceded this read as a 2019 list with no touch
    surface). NO group carries a label: a "Library" caption over
    Bookmarks/History/Safe Folder shipped for a day and was cut on sight
    (maintainer: "why library title?") — three rows whose glyphs and
    names already say what they are need no heading, and the other two
    groups never had one. The two icon rows sit in a card of their own.
    Three rows of these groups can HIDE (Translate, Quit, and Safe Folder
    swaps to Downloads), so the corners are recomputed from the VISIBLE
    rows by SheetGroups.applyCorners after every toggle; the XML shapes
    are only the common-case default.

    Shape (top→bottom):
      1. Drag handle (shared include).                    [pinned]
      2. Site-identity row: favicon + page title +        [pinned]
         hostname. Same identity vocabulary the
         SecuritySheet uses, scoped to "act on this
         page". Stays pinned — it's the anchor, scrolling
         the title away would lose the context the rest
         of the rows act on. Dismiss is swipe-down or
         scrim-tap; no inline X — the drag handle and the
         taller header read clearly enough as a sheet,
         and dropping the X also drops a second dismiss
         affordance that did the same job.
      3. ─── scroll boundary ───
      4. Quick-action CARD (one non-clickable card, same inset and
         surface as the groups below) holding
           Controls icon row:     Back · Forward · Bookmark★ · Refresh
           Page-actions icon row: Find · Desktop · Share · Save
         (the two icon rows are one action block, so one card)
      6. Tabs     card group — New tab, New private tab, Translate
      7. Library  card group — Bookmarks, History, Safe Folder (no label)
      8. System   card group — Cloud, Settings, optional Quit

    The Bookmark★ star is the promoted bookmark toggle; there is no
    longer a "Bookmark page" list row (its add/edit both live on the
    star now).

    Row anatomy:
      • a Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard holding ONE
        Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText: 56dp, 16dp gutter — the M3
        one-line list item, shared with the Home popup and the
        OptionsAdapter sheets so every menu row in the app reads at
        the same rhythm; icon + single line
      • drawableStartCompat icon at 16dp drawablePadding, TitleMedium /
        16sp text (M3 list-item headline size), onSurfaceVariant
      • No trailing element on any list row — the card's ripple is enough

    State handling stays in the fragment:
      • Bookmark STAR (controls icon row, not this list) flips its
        icon/label/tint between outline·"Bookmark" and filled·amber
        ·"Saved" based on mHasBookmark, and toggles the bookmark in
        place (add/delete on the shared repository) with an Edit/Undo
        confirmation toast — see applyStarState / onBookmarkStarClicked.
      • Both icon rows drop to icon-only together past a width/font-scale
        breakpoint (QuickRowLabels.iconOnly + a post-measure fit check);
        icons never move.
      • Desktop icon (page-actions row) highlights in the accent tint
        when the tab is in desktop mode (applyDesktopState).
      • Vault row swaps to Downloads in incognito (icon + label +
        dispatched id).
      • Quit row stays GONE unless SETTINGS_QUIT_PREF is on; the row
        uses colorPrimary text + tint so the destructive treatment
        matches Downloads' / Bookmarks' Delete row.
-->
<!--
    Root: the sheet HUGS its content — it opens exactly as tall as the rows
    need rather than being forced to fill up to the toolbar (which left dead
    space below the short two-icon-row menu). The FrameLayout + popup_content +
    NestedScrollView are all wrap_content, so there is NO minimum height.

    The MAXIMUM is the height the Capture sheet occupies — everything below the
    toolbar — NOT the shared 640dp bottom_sheet_max_height dimen. It is enforced
    on popup_content's layout height by
    PopupBrowserSheetDialogFragment.applyContentMaxHeight(), which writes the cap
    only when the measured content actually exceeds it; the behaviour-level cap
    (resolveMaxHeightPx) is an outer guard and is NOT sufficient on its own — a
    capped wrapper around a wrap_content child still measured full height, which
    is why the sheet rendered full-screen on-device. The guard is the content
    cap PLUS the root's nav-bar padding (the base adds it): applied bare, it
    took the inset out of popup_content's EXACT height — the sheet opened one
    inset below the toolbar and clipped Settings under the gesture bar.

    Ceiling only: it never pads a short menu out to that height. Past the cap the
    pinned identity header stays put and the weighted scroller below it scrolls.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/popup_content"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:orientation="vertical">

    <include
        layout="@layout/dialog_drag_handle" />


    <!-- Site identity. Mirrors the SecuritySheet's identity block
         (favicon + title + host) so the two sheets read as siblings
         on the browser surface. Renders taller than the menu rows
         (minHeight 72dp via 12dp vertical padding) so it reads as a
         header, not just another list row. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/popup_identity"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:minHeight="72dp"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingHorizontal="16dp"
        android:paddingVertical="12dp">

        <!-- 40dp tinted surface tile with the 24dp favicon centred
             inside (8dp padding → 24dp content). DuckDuckGo-style
             frame so transparent / monochrome / oddly-cropped
             favicons still read as a single identity chip rather
             than floating on the sheet. -->
        <androidx.appcompat.widget.AppCompatImageView
            android:id="@+id/popup_identity_favicon"
            android:layout_width="40dp"
            android:layout_height="40dp"
            android:layout_marginEnd="16dp"
            android:background="@drawable/bg_popup_favicon"
            android:contentDescription="@null"
            android:padding="8dp"
            android:scaleType="centerInside"
            tools:src="@drawable/ic_firedown" />

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/popup_identity_title"
                style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleSmall.Emphasized"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                tools:text="EL PAÍS: el periódico global" />

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/popup_identity_host"
                style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.BodyMedium"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                tools:text="elpais.com" />

        </LinearLayout>

    </LinearLayout>


    <androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:overScrollMode="never">

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingBottom="8dp">


            <!-- Row 1: transient chrome controls (Back · Forward ·
                 Bookmark★ · Refresh). -->
            <!-- The two icon rows sit in ONE non-clickable card, the same
                 surface and inset as the row groups below: a flat icon grid
                 over grouped cards read as two different menus stacked (the
                 grid looked like it belonged to the identity header above,
                 not to the menu). The card is a GROUND, not a row — no click,
                 no ripple of its own; each button keeps its own. Its 16dp
                 inset narrows the four columns by 32dp, which
                 QuickRowLabels.ROW_HORIZONTAL_PADDING_DP accounts for. -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_quick_card"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                android:layout_marginHorizontal="16dp"
                android:layout_marginTop="0dp"
                android:clickable="false"
                android:focusable="false"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupSingle">

            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:paddingVertical="4dp">

            <include
                layout="@layout/fragment_dialog_browser_popup_header"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content" />


            <!-- Row 2: page actions (Find · Desktop · Share · Save), the
                 former "This page" list group collapsed into an icon row that
                 mirrors the controls row above. NO divider between the two
                 rows — they read as one action block, bounded by the identity
                 divider above and the divider below. Plain MaterialButtons
                 (not BrowserButton subclasses): each dispatches its id like the
                 old text rows did; the fragment folds them into the same
                 icon-only fit logic and paints Desktop's active tint. Short
                 android:text (fits 4-up) + full android:contentDescription
                 (TalkBack/tooltip). -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_actions_row"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingTop="2dp"
                android:paddingHorizontal="@dimen/quick_row_horizontal_padding">

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/popup_find"
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.PopupQuickRowButton"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/browser_menu_find_in_page"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_find_short"
                    app:icon="@drawable/ic_search_24" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/popup_desktop"
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.PopupQuickRowButton"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/browser_menu_desktop_site"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_desktop_short"
                    app:icon="@drawable/ic_computer_24" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/popup_share"
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.PopupQuickRowButton"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/browser_menu_share"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_share"
                    app:icon="@drawable/ic_share_24" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/popup_save_snapshot"
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.PopupQuickRowButton"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/browser_menu_save_snapshot"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_save_short"
                    app:icon="@drawable/ic_baseline_archive_24" />

            </LinearLayout>

            </LinearLayout>

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>


            <!-- ── Tabs ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_section_tabs"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetGroup"
                android:layout_marginHorizontal="16dp">

            <!-- New tab — always opens a REGULAR tab (dispatches
                 R.id.new_tab, which BrowserFragment forces to
                 non-incognito), so from incognito chrome this is the
                 explicit exit-to-normal-tab action. Mirrors the
                 fixed-meaning rows browsers like Chrome/Firefox show. -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_new_tab"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupTop">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/popup_tabs_new"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_tabs_new_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            <!-- New private tab — always opens an INCOGNITO tab
                 (dispatches R.id.new_incognito_tab). Fixed meaning in
                 both modes, matching the New tab row above. -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_new_incognito_tab"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupMiddle">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/open_new_private_tab_2"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_incognito_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            <!-- Translate page ↔ Show original — Gecko's built-in translator.
                 A text row in THIS group, after the tab rows: it first shipped
                 as a lone row wedged between the page-actions icon grid and the
                 divider, which read as a stray (rejected on-device). Not a
                 fifth icon either (the grid's icon-only fit is tuned for four).
                 One row, two meanings: the label and the dispatched action
                 follow the tab's translation state (bound in bindRows). Hidden
                 on non-web documents and when the feature is switched off —
                 and then the row above takes the group's bottom corners
                 (SheetGroups.applyCorners, called after bindTranslateRow). -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_translate"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupBottom">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/popup_translate_text"
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_translate"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/translate_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- ── Library ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_section_library"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetGroup"
                android:layout_marginHorizontal="16dp">

            <!-- Bookmarks. -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_bookmarks"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupTop">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/library_bookmarks"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_bookmarks_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            <!-- History. -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_history"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupMiddle">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/library_history"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_history_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            <!-- Vault (Downloads in incognito; the fragment
                 repaints drawableStart + label + dispatched id). -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_vault"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupBottom">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/popup_vault_text"
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/navigation_vault"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_lock_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- ── System ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_section_system"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetGroup"
                android:layout_marginHorizontal="16dp">

            <!-- Sync — bookmarks + encrypted download backup (one account). -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_sync"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupTop">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/settings_account_title"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/cloud_outline_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            <!-- Settings. -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_settings"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupBottom">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_settings"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_settings_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            <!-- Destructive Quit — GONE unless SETTINGS_QUIT_PREF
                 is on. colorPrimary text + drawable tint is what
                 differentiates it. When it shows, Settings loses the
                 group's bottom corners to it (applyQuitVisibility →
                 SheetGroups.applyCorners). -->
            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                android:id="@+id/popup_quit"
                style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowCard"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible"
                app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearanceOverlay.FireDown.SheetGroupBottom">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/Firedown.Widget.SheetRowText.Final"
                    android:text="@string/delete_browsing_data_on_quit_action"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_logout_24" />

            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            </LinearLayout>

        </LinearLayout>

    </androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>

    </LinearLayout>

</FrameLayout>
